    <!-- ===================== HERO ===================== -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container hero__inner">
        <p class="hero__eyebrow">Private Water Supplies</p>
        <h1 class="hero__title">
          Stop paying for water<br>
          <span class="em">you could own.</span>
        </h1>
        <div class="hero__scroll" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="hero__scroll-arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 4v15M6 13l6 6 6-6"/>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="hero__lead">
          <p class="hero__lead-lg">
            A private water supply puts your property on its own source. Reliable, high-quality
            water, free of rising utility charges and unaffected by mains failures.
          </p>
          <p class="hero__lead-sm">
            The catch: doing this properly is not a job for generalists. We only work on bespoke
            systems, designed around your own water chemistry, installed by our own engineers rather
            than subcontractors, and personally maintained for as long as you need us.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- The pair the home hero has carried since the rebuild, in the same
             order: the thing you want them to do, then the number for someone
             who has landed mid-crisis. Until now a service page asked for
             nothing until the footer, and the first pressable thing on it was
             inside a closed accordion panel six screens down. -->
        <div class="hero__actions">
          <a class="btn-inquiry btn-inquiry--lg" href="/enquiry/">Book a site survey <span class="btn-inquiry__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a>
          <a class="btn-line btn-line--lg" href="tel:{{ site.tel }}" aria-label="Call the 24-hour emergency line on {{ site.phone }}">24hr emergency: {{ site.phone }}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ WHY IT MATTERS (dark) ============
      Rides off the hero on the same navy, under a divider, so the page answers
      "why would I want this" before it shows a photograph. See service-why.njk.
    -->
{% include "service-why.njk" %}

    <!-- ============ TRUST: THE LOGOS, EARLY ============
      A B2B reader's first question after "what is this" is "who else trusts
      you", and until now the answer was seven screens down, below the sectors.
      This is the earliest place it can go. It cannot sit between the hero and
      the why-cards: those two share the navy deliberately, the hairline at the
      top of service-why is what separates them, and `.hero:has(+ .service-why)`
      pays for the gap above that rule — a section spliced between them breaks
      the adjacency and the spacing with it. The marks also need a pale ground;
      they are dark ink at 72% and would vanish on the navy.

      So: straight after the why-cards, where the surface changes anyway, and
      before the photographic band. No closing hairline now that the figures
      are no longer directly beneath it.
    -->
    {% set clientsId = "pws-clients" %}
    {% set clientsClass = "clients--airy" %}
    {% set clientsSurface = "section--paper" %}
    {% include "clients.njk" %}

    <!-- ============ PROJECT BAND + SERVICES (the reveal pair) ============
      Same pairing as every other service page: the band pins inside the wrapper
      and the light section climbs over it. See service-band.njk.
    -->
    <div class="reveal">
{% include "service-band.njk" %}

    <!-- ===================== SERVICES (light) ===================== -->
    <section class="section section--paper services" aria-labelledby="services-title">
      <div class="container">

        <h2 id="services-title" class="statement">
          From first survey
          <span class="em">to final commissioning.</span>
        </h2>

        <div class="accordion">
          {# OPEN. Six collapsed panels meant a reader who never clicked saw
             none of the process, and the panels hold the best copy on the page.
             The first one open shows what the pattern is and what is in it. #}
          <details class="acc" open>
            <summary class="acc__head">
              <span class="acc__title">Site Survey &amp; Water Analysis</span>
              <span class="acc__toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="acc__body">
              <div class="acc__media">
                <img src="/assets/t-elstead-6784.webp" alt="Parkland with a mature oak, a greenhouse and a farmhouse beyond, and an open borehole chamber in the foreground." width="1536" height="1024" loading="eager">
              </div>
              <div class="acc__copy">
                <p>Every private supply starts with a site survey and a UKAS-accredited water
                  analysis. No system gets specified before we know exactly what's coming out of the
                  ground, flow rate, depth, and the full chemistry of the source water.</p>
                <a class="btn-inquiry" href="/enquiry/">Book a site survey <span class="btn-inquiry__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="acc">
            <summary class="acc__head">
              <span class="acc__title">Bespoke System Design</span>
              <span class="acc__toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="acc__body">
              <div class="acc__media">
                <img src="/assets/b-estate-4933.webp" alt="A control panel designed and built in-house, with indicator lights and selector switches for the borehole, soft and potable tanks." width="1536" height="1024" loading="eager">
              </div>
              <div class="acc__copy">
                <p>We design the filtration, storage and pumping to match your source and your
                  property's demand. Everything specified is chosen for reliability and long service
                  life, a system built to run quietly and reliably.</p>
                <a class="btn-inquiry" href="/enquiry/">Get a system specified <span class="btn-inquiry__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="acc">
            <summary class="acc__head">
              <span class="acc__title">Filtration &amp; Treatment</span>
              <span class="acc__toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="acc__body">
              <div class="acc__media">
                <img src="/assets/l-mill-5576.webp" alt="A plant room with a UV steriliser, cartridge filters, a blue pressure vessel and pipework on plywood walls." width="1536" height="1024" loading="eager">
              </div>
              <div class="acc__copy">
                <p>Treatment is built around your water's chemistry, iron and manganese reduction,
                  pH correction, and UV sterilisation where required. The result is water treated to
                  a standard mains supply rarely matches.</p>
                <a class="btn-inquiry" href="/enquiry/">Get your water analysed <span class="btn-inquiry__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="acc">
            <summary class="acc__head">
              <span class="acc__title">Installation</span>
              <span class="acc__toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="acc__body">
              <div class="acc__media">
                <img src="/assets/lk-effingham-8608.webp" alt="An installed plant room with a black storage tank, a wall-mounted control panel, twin pumps and labelled pipework." width="1536" height="1024" loading="eager">
              </div>
              <div class="acc__copy">
                <p>Our own engineers install every system, never subcontracted. The plant is set out
                  cleanly, commissioned properly, and left in a state we'd be happy to return to in
                  ten years' time.</p>
                <a class="btn-inquiry" href="/enquiry/">Get a fixed-price quote <span class="btn-inquiry__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="acc">
            <summary class="acc__head">
              <span class="acc__title">Commissioning &amp; Handover</span>
              <span class="acc__toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="acc__body">
              <div class="acc__media">
                <img src="/assets/uppark-4882.webp" alt="A commissioned control panel beside framed commissioning notices, a water meter and a tank float." width="1536" height="1024" loading="eager">
              </div>
              <div class="acc__copy">
                <p>The system is tested to specification, documented, and explained to whoever will
                  use it. You're left with current compliance evidence and a clear understanding of
                  how your supply works.</p>
                <a class="btn-inquiry" href="/enquiry/">Talk to an engineer <span class="btn-inquiry__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="acc">
            <summary class="acc__head">
              <span class="acc__title">Servicing &amp; Maintenance</span>
              <span class="acc__toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="acc__body">
              <div class="acc__media">
                <img src="/assets/s-farm-4835.webp" alt="A borehole headworks board on a garden wall: pump controller, filter housing, expansion vessel and valves." width="1536" height="1024" loading="eager">
              </div>
              <div class="acc__copy">
                <p>Regular maintenance visits keep the system operating at spec, with annual UKAS
                  re-testing. Existing service clients have direct access to our engineers on a
                  24-hour emergency line, same number, same team, no call centre, and in most cases
                  we are on site within four hours of the call.</p>
                <a class="btn-inquiry" href="/enquiry/">Get a servicing quote <span class="btn-inquiry__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    </div><!-- /.reveal -->

    <!-- ===================== POSITIONING (dark) =====================
      NOT the retired "Sectors". The client asked for sectors removed from the
      site completely (11/08/26) and /index.njk lost its typographic sectors
      list then, but that was a navigation section standing on its own. These
      four cards are examples of the property types a private supply suits, on
      the page about private supplies, and they answer the question a reader
      actually arrives with: is this for something like mine. They stay.
      (Removed once on 21/09/26 by reading the 11/08 instruction too widely,
      and put straight back. Don't do it again.)

      What the section was missing was the middle beat. The heading makes a
      claim, "we only work bespoke, not to a price list", and the cards below
      say who we make them for; nothing in between said what bespoke actually
      BUYS you. It does now, in the lead: a fixed price, after a survey and an
      analysis of your own water. That fact was true before and was buried in
      the FAQ, seven screens down.

      It went in .positioning__note first, the second grid column that was
      styled and had never been filled, and it looked wrong there: quiet grey
      type marooned at the top of a tall empty column, reading as an aside
      rather than as the point. One column, one argument.
    -->
    <section class="section positioning" aria-labelledby="positioning-title">
      <div class="container">

        <h2 id="positioning-title" class="statement">
          We only work on bespoke systems,
          <span class="em">not price lists.</span>
        </h2>

        <div class="positioning__intro">
          <p class="positioning__lead">
            Invicta has looked after private water supplies across Surrey, Sussex and the wider
            South East for over twenty years. No catalogue systems and no ballpark figures: every
            quote is fixed-price, after a site survey and a UKAS-accredited analysis of your own
            water.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="sectors">
          <article class="sector">
            <h3>Landed estates</h3>
            <p>High-volume private supplies serving multiple properties and estate operations from a
              single, well-understood source.</p>
            <div class="sector__media parallax">
              <img src="/assets/b-estate-0416.webp" alt="A Tudor brick tower on a Sussex estate, with a lawn and a timber outbuilding beside it." style="object-position: 68% center" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy">
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="sector">
            <h3>Country houses</h3>
            <p>Independent water for rural homes off the mains, or with a connection they would
              rather not depend on.</p>
            <div class="sector__media parallax">
              <img src="/assets/img-0428.webp" alt="A red brick country house with tall chimneys across a wide lawn." width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy">
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="sector">
            <h3>Institutions</h3>
            <p>Reliable, compliant supply for schools, clubs, sporting venues and commercial sites
              with demanding requirements.</p>
            <div class="sector__media parallax">
              <img src="/assets/img-1133.webp" alt="A large grey-clad commercial building under construction, with pipework in the trench at its base." width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy">
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="sector">
            <h3>New-build developments</h3>
            <p>New mains and private supplies designed in from the start of a development, not bolted
              on after.</p>
            <div class="sector__media parallax">
              <img src="/assets/s-cottage-5641.webp" alt="A new-build house in timber and stone, with the ground around it freshly graded." style="object-position: 40% center" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy">
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ THE FIGURES ============
      This used to be the second half of a LOGOS + RULE + FIGURES pair, on the
      argument that a sceptic reads "who trusts you" before "how much have you
      done". The order was right; the position was not. Both halves sat seven
      screens down, so a reader deciding whether to carry on past the hero had
      no proof at all. The logos have gone up to sit under the why-cards and
      the figures stay here, where they back the case studies that follow.
      The band lost its closing hairline with its partner.
    -->
    {# The shared band, so this page quotes the same figures as every other. It
       used to carry its own numbered, picture-less variant with a different
       year count on it. #}
    {% include "stats-band.njk" %}

    <!-- ============ CASE STUDIES (one per screen, light) ============ -->
    {% set studies = [] %}
    {% for cs in caseStudies %}{% if "private-water-supplies" in cs.services %}{% set _ = studies.push(cs) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    {% set carouselId = "pws" %}
    {% set bentoSurface = "section--light" %}
    {% set carouselTitle = "Supplies we've designed <span class='em'>and delivered.</span>" %}
    {% set carouselLead = "Two failed boreholes, three sources feeding one house, and an inherited system that finally passed its EHO test." %}
    {% include "case-bento.njk" %}

    <!-- ===================== FAQ (dark) ===================== -->
    <section class="section faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="container faq__grid">
        <aside class="faq__aside">
          <h2 id="faq-title" class="faq__title">Frequently asked.</h2>
          <p class="faq__intro">The questions we hear most often from clients thinking about a private
            supply. If yours isn't answered here, get in touch, we'll answer plainly.</p>
        </aside>

        {# ORDER IS DELIBERATE. Permission first, because it decides whether
           this is even possible on the site; cost SECOND, because on a
           five-figure bespoke install it is what everyone wants next, and it
           used to be answered last, below five questions nobody had asked yet.
           The answer is a good one and it was doing no work down there: there
           is no typical figure, and the quote is fixed-price after a survey. #}
        <div class="faq__list">
          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary class="faq__q">
              Do I need permission to install a borehole?
              <svg class="faq__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="faq__a">In most cases, no formal planning permission is required, though water
              abstraction over 20 cubic metres per day requires a licence from the Environment Agency.
              We handle the paperwork and liaison as part of any install where it's needed.</p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary class="faq__q">
              What does a typical install cost?
              <svg class="faq__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="faq__a">Every install is bespoke, so there is no typical figure. Costs depend on
              source depth, water chemistry, storage requirements and property demand. We provide a
              fixed-price quote after a site survey.</p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary class="faq__q">
              How long does a borehole and treatment system last?
              <svg class="faq__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="faq__a">A properly designed and installed system will run for 25–40 years with
              routine maintenance. Filtration media and UV lamps are consumables replaced on a service
              schedule. The borehole itself, the pump housing, and the treatment vessels are all
              long-life.</p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary class="faq__q">
              How often does the water need testing?
              <svg class="faq__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="faq__a">Annually as standard, though we recommend more frequent testing if your
              source water is known to be variable. All testing goes through a UKAS-accredited
              laboratory.</p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary class="faq__q">
              What happens if something goes wrong outside working hours?
              <svg class="faq__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="faq__a">Existing service clients have direct access to our engineers on a 24-hour
              emergency line. In most cases we can get to site within four hours of the call.</p>
          </details>

          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary class="faq__q">
              Can you take over servicing a system installed by someone else?
              <svg class="faq__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="faq__a">Yes, provided the system is safe to work on and we can access the plant.
              We start with a full inspection and water analysis, then propose any remedial work needed
              before taking on the ongoing service contract.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    
